---
import g from '../../../sources/site-experiments/feed-gate-preview.json';
import LiveCta from './LiveCta.astro';
import './preview.css';
---
<figure class="pv" aria-labelledby="gb-cap">
  <p class="pv-tag mono" id="gb-cap"><b>BUILD-COMPUTED</b> · stored Python reference run, checked against the browser runtime in tests · synthetic records</p>
  <h3>A timestamp that cannot be true</h3>
  <p>Record 1 arrives at <b>21 ms</b> but claims it was available at <b>19 ms</b>. The project's actual archive validator rejects it:</p>
  <pre class="mono failure">ValueError: {g.error}</pre>
  <p>In the corrected fixture, <code>available_ms</code> is <b>22</b>. The same Python function returns these book rows:</p>
  <div class="preview-scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Record</th><th>Available (ms)</th><th>State</th><th>Bid size (units)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{g.rows.map((r) => (<tr><td>{r.sequence}</td><td>{r.available_ms}</td><td>{r.status}</td><td>{r.bid_size / 100}</td></tr>))}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="limit">The update replaces the aggregate size; it does not add another order. These are declared test clocks. Passing this check does not authenticate timestamps or validate a strategy.</p>
  <p><a href={g.source.files['replay/admission.py'].url}>Exact Python source</a> · <a href={g.source.files['test_admission.py'].url}>Upstream boundary tests</a></p>
  <LiveCta id="gatedbuild" what="edit the record, execute this Python validator, and inspect the returned evidence" />
</figure>
<style>
  h3 { margin-top: 4px; }
  .failure { padding: 14px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: var(--bg); border-left: 3px solid var(--down); font-size: 0.875rem; }
  .preview-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  th,td { padding: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-2); text-align: left; }
  .limit { color: var(--muted); }
</style>
